.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt MOXYFILE 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm moxyfile
.Nd configuration file for moxy
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the configuration file for
.Xr moxy 1 .
It uses TOML format and controls which child MCP servers are spawned,
how their capabilities are aggregated, and per-server behavior options
like ephemeral mode, annotation filtering, and pagination.
.Sh FILE HIERARCHY
Configuration files are loaded and merged in order:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Pa ~/.config/moxy/moxyfile
(global).
.It
Each parent directory between
.Ev HOME
and the current working directory.
.It
.Pa ./moxyfile
(project-local).
.El
.Pp
Later files override earlier ones.
Servers are matched by name: a same-named server in an overlay replaces
the base server entirely.
New servers from overlays are appended.
Top-level boolean flags are replaced if present in the overlay.
.Va disable-moxins
and
.Va disable-servers
entries are merged additively: each layer appends to the disabled set.
.Va allow-tools
lists are intersected: each layer that sets one can only shorten it.
.Pp
A moxyfile may also pull in additional moxyfiles from arbitrary paths with
the
.Va include
key (see
.Sx TOP-LEVEL KEYS ) .
Each included file is merged just before the file that includes it, so an
include supplies defaults that the including file \(em and the rest of the
hierarchy above it \(em can still override.
This reaches configuration kept outside the
.Ev HOME Ns \(-> Ns Pa CWD
walk, e.g. a checkout mounted at a top-level path.
.Sh TOP-LEVEL KEYS
.Bl -tag -width "progressive-disclosure"
.It Va ephemeral
When set to
.Cm true ,
servers without an explicit
.Va ephemeral
setting are treated as ephemeral by default.
Optional.
Default:
.Cm false .
.It Va progressive-disclosure
When set to
.Cm true ,
enables progressive disclosure for servers without an explicit setting.
Optional.
Default:
.Cm false .
.It Va builtin-native
When set to
.Cm false ,
the system moxin directory (the moxins that ship with moxy, baked into the
build) is not appended to the moxin search path.
Moxins found via
.Ev MOXIN_PATH
are unaffected, including a
.Ev MOXIN_PATH
entry that itself points at a system moxin directory.
Honoured by
.Sy serve mcp ,
.Sy serve-http ,
.Sy restart
and
.Sy status .
Unlike the additive disable lists, the closest moxyfile that sets it wins,
so a project moxyfile with
.Cm true
overrides a global
.Cm false .
To hide one system moxin while keeping the rest, put a same-named moxin
earlier on
.Ev MOXIN_PATH
(it shadows the system copy) or use
.Va disable-moxins .
See
.Xr moxin 7
DISCOVERY.
Optional.
Default:
.Cm true .
.It Va disable-moxins
Array of moxin names or
.Dq name.tool
pairs to suppress.
A bare name (e.g.\&
.Dq chix )
hides the entire moxin server.
A dotted pair (e.g.\&
.Dq man.semantic-search )
hides a single tool within a moxin while leaving the rest visible.
Only affects moxins (from
.Ev MOXIN_PATH
or the system moxin directory);
moxyfile-configured servers are unaffected.
Matching is by name, so a bare name hides every copy of that moxin, whichever
directory it came from.
Entries are merged additively across the hierarchy.
Optional.
Default: empty.
.It Va disable-servers
Array of
.Sx SERVERS
names to suppress, e.g.\&
.Dq dodder .
Whole-server only \(em dotted entries are rejected at parse time because
.Sx SERVERS
tool lists come from the runtime initialize handshake rather than static
config.
A disabled server name still occupies the namespace, so a moxin with the
same name remains shadowed (consistent with the normal collision rule).
Entries are merged additively across the hierarchy, so a layer can add
disables but not re-enable a server disabled by a higher-priority layer.
Optional.
Default: empty.
.It Va allow-tools
Array of the only names that exist.
A bare name allows every tool of that server or moxin
.Pq e.g.\& Dq smith ,
or one of
.Xr moxy 1 Ap s
own meta tools by its name
.Pq e.g.\& Dq restart ;
a dotted pair
.Pq e.g.\& Dq grit.status
allows a single tool.
Anything not named is neither listed nor callable, including the meta tools
.Pq Li restart , batch , async No and the rest
and including tools of
.Sx SERVERS
entries, which the disable lists cannot reach one by one.
Where the disable lists hide what is named and so let through a tool a server
grows later, this key lets through nothing it does not name.
.Pp
Unset means everything is allowed.
An empty array is set, and allows nothing.
Across the hierarchy the lists intersect: the first file to set the key
establishes the list and every later file can only take entries away, with a
bare name narrowed by a dotted pair under it
.Po
.Dq grit
then
.Dq grit.status
leaves
.Dq grit.status
.Pc .
A file that does not set the key leaves the list as it found it.
It governs tools only; resources and prompts are unaffected.
Entries name tools as
.Ar server Ns Li \&. Ns Ar tool
whatever
.Fl -name-template
is in force.
Optional.
Default: unset.
.It Va include
Array of paths to additional moxyfiles to merge.
A leading
.Pa ~/
and
.Ev $VAR
references are expanded; a relative path is resolved against the directory
of the including file.
Each included file is merged just before the file that declares the include,
in listed order, so includes act as defaults the including file can override.
Included files may themselves declare
.Va include ;
an include cycle (a file that reaches itself, directly or transitively) is
reported as an error rather than followed.
Optional.
Default: empty.
.It Va credentials
Table of three commands,
.Va read ,
.Va write
and
.Va delete ,
that store OAuth tokens for
.Va url
servers;
.Li {name}
in a command is replaced with the server name.
Optional.
Default: the system keychain.
.El
.Sh SERVERS
Each server is defined as an array-of-tables entry:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[[servers]]
name = "grit"
command = "grit mcp"
.Ed
.Ss Required fields
.Bl -tag -width "command"
.It Va name
Unique identifier for the server.
Must not contain dots
.Pq dots are used as the namespace separator .
May contain hyphens.
.It Va command
Shell command to spawn the server.
See
.Sx COMMAND FORMAT
below.
.El
.Ss Optional fields
.Bl -tag -width "progressive-disclosure"
.It Va ephemeral
When
.Cm true ,
the server is not kept running.
Moxy probes it at startup to discover capabilities, shuts it down,
and re-spawns it on demand for each tool call.
Overrides the global
.Va ephemeral
setting.
.It Va progressive-disclosure
Overrides the global
.Va progressive-disclosure
setting for this server.
.It Va paginate
When
.Cm true ,
enables cursor-based pagination for this server's resource lists.
Default:
.Cm false .
.It Va generate-resource-tools
When
.Cm true ,
generates synthetic
.Cm resource-read
and
.Cm resource-templates
tools for this server, allowing tool-only clients to access resources.
.It Va nix-devshell
Flake reference to a Nix devshell.
When set, the effective command becomes:
.Dl nix develop Ar ref Li --command Ar command args ...
.Pp
See
.Sx NIX DEVSHELL
below.
.It Va url
Address of a streamable-HTTP MCP server to connect to, in place of
.Va command .
A server has one or the other, never both.
.It Va headers
Table of HTTP headers sent to a
.Va url
server.
.Li $VAR
references in the values are expanded from the environment when the server is
connected.
.It Va headers-helper
Command run to produce further headers for a
.Va url
server; it prints a JSON object of header names to values.
.It Va oauth
Table with
.Va client-id
and
.Va callback-port
for a
.Va url
server that authenticates with OAuth.
.El
.Sh COMMAND FORMAT
The
.Va command
field accepts two forms.
.Pp
String form (split on whitespace):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
command = "grit mcp --verbose"
.Ed
.Pp
Array form (preserved as-is):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
command = ["grit", "mcp", "--verbose"]
.Ed
.Pp
The first element is the executable; remaining elements are arguments.
Empty commands are invalid.
.Sh ANNOTATIONS
Annotation filters restrict which tools are exposed from a child server
based on MCP tool annotation hints.
They can be specified as a sub-table or as flat fields at the server level.
.Pp
Sub-table form:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[[servers]]
name = "grit"
command = "grit mcp"

[servers.annotations]
readOnlyHint = true
.Ed
.Pp
Flat form:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[[servers]]
name = "grit"
command = "grit mcp"
readOnlyHint = true
.Ed
.Pp
Available annotation fields:
.Bl -tag -width "destructiveHint"
.It Va readOnlyHint
Only expose tools marked as read-only.
.It Va destructiveHint
Only expose tools marked as destructive.
.It Va idempotentHint
Only expose tools marked as idempotent.
.It Va openWorldHint
Only expose tools marked as open-world.
.El
.Pp
All annotation fields are optional.
When set, only tools whose annotations match the specified value are exposed.
.Sh NIX DEVSHELL
The
.Va nix-devshell
field wraps the server command inside a Nix development shell.
.Pp
Given:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[[servers]]
name = "example"
command = "myserver --verbose"
nix-devshell = "github:org/repo"
.Ed
.Pp
The effective command becomes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nix develop github:org/repo --command myserver --verbose
.Ed
.Pp
Valid flake references include
.Dq \&.
(current directory),
.Dq github:org/repo ,
and
.Dq github:org/repo?dir=path/to/subflake .
.Sh NARROWING
The hierarchy merge above lets a closer file add to what a farther one
configured: it may add servers, replace a server's command, or turn the system
moxins back on.
That is right for one person's own directories and wrong for a process that
hands a toolset to another.
A spawner must not give a child more than it holds itself, so a second relation
exists alongside the merge.
A child moxyfile
.Em narrows
a parent when it grants nothing the parent does not.
.Pp
Narrowing compares
.Em effective
configurations \(em each side fully merged, with its includes resolved \(em never
one file against another.
It compares what is written, not what it expands to:
.Li $VAR
references in
.Va command
and
.Va headers
are compared as the literal text, and nothing is read from the environment.
.Xr moxy 1
.Cm show-effective-moxyfile
writes a configuration in the same unexpanded form, so a parent reference
never contains an expanded secret and is safe to write to disk.
.Pp
The relation, key by key:
.Bl -tag -width "disable-servers"
.It Sx SERVERS
Every server the child runs must be a server the parent runs, with the same
invocation.
A server
.Dq runs
when it is defined and not named in that side's
.Va disable-servers .
The invocation is
.Va command
.Pq compared argument by argument, so one argument containing a space is not two arguments ,
.Va url ,
.Va headers ,
.Va headers-helper ,
.Va oauth
and
.Va nix-devshell .
The child may leave a server out.
It may not add one, change one, or run one the parent has disabled.
.Pp
An annotation filter restricts a server, so the child must keep every hint the
parent sets, with the same value, and may set more.
.Pp
.Va ephemeral ,
.Va progressive-disclosure ,
.Va paginate
and
.Va generate-resource-tools
change how a server is presented, not what it can do, and are not compared.
.It Va disable-moxins
The child must disable everything the parent disables.
A parent entry for one tool
.Pq Dq man.semantic-search
is satisfied by the same entry or by the whole moxin
.Pq Dq man ;
a parent entry for a whole moxin is satisfied only by that entry.
The child may disable more.
.Pp
One further case: a
.Sx SERVERS
entry hides the moxin of the same name, even while the server is disabled.
A child that leaves out a server the parent defines must therefore name it in
.Va disable-moxins ,
or the moxin the parent could never reach would appear.
.It Va allow-tools
If the parent sets an allowlist the child must set one too, and every child
entry must be covered by a parent entry: the same entry, or for a dotted pair
the parent's bare name.
A child that leaves the key unset under a parent that sets it would allow
everything, and is refused.
If the parent sets none, the child may set any.
.It Va disable-servers
Not compared on its own; it decides which servers run, above.
.It Va builtin-native
If the parent's effective value is
.Cm false ,
the child's must be
.Cm false
too.
Unset counts as
.Cm true .
This is the one place narrowing contradicts the merge, where the closest file
wins.
.It Va credentials
If the child sets a
.Li [credentials]
table it must equal the parent's.
The child may leave it out.
.It Va include
Resolved before the comparison; whatever an include brings in is judged by the
rules above.
.It Va ephemeral , progressive-disclosure
Not rights; not compared.
.El
.Pp
Two things a moxyfile cannot say, and narrowing therefore cannot judge:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Which moxin directories are searched.
That is
.Ev MOXIN_PATH ,
and a moxin's tools and their permission tiers
.Pq Va perms-request , see Xr moxin 7
come from whichever directory wins.
A child given a different
.Ev MOXIN_PATH
can reach a same-named moxin with looser tiers while its moxyfile narrows
perfectly.
Whoever launches the child must give it the parent's
.Ev MOXIN_PATH .
.It
The
.Cm serve-http
flags
.Fl -expose
and
.Fl -name-template ,
and what a
.Li $VAR
expands to.
These belong to the command line and environment of the child process.
.El
.Pp
.Xr moxy 1
.Cm narrows
checks the relation for two references and prints one line per violation.
Setting
.Ev MOXY_PARENT_MOXYFILE
makes a serving
.Xr moxy 1
enforce it on itself, at startup and on every reload.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Minimal configuration with a single server:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[[servers]]
name = "grit"
command = "grit mcp"
.Ed
.Pp
Multiple servers with annotation filtering:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[[servers]]
name = "grit"
command = "grit mcp"
paginate = true

[servers.annotations]
readOnlyHint = true

[[servers]]
name = "dodder"
command = ["dodder", "mcp"]
generate-resource-tools = true
.Ed
.Pp
Ephemeral servers spawned on demand:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ephemeral = true

[[servers]]
name = "chix"
command = "chix serve"

[[servers]]
name = "grit"
command = "grit mcp"
ephemeral = false
.Ed
.Pp
In this example,
.Dq chix
inherits the global ephemeral setting while
.Dq grit
overrides it to stay persistent.
.Pp
Disabling specific moxins and individual tools:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
disable-moxins = ["chix", "man.semantic-search"]
.Ed
.Pp
This hides the entire
.Dq chix
moxin and the
.Dq semantic-search
tool from the
.Dq man
moxin.
Other tools in
.Dq man
remain visible.
.Pp
Disabling configured
.Sx SERVERS
entries (e.g. for a per-directory laptop where some globally configured
servers are not relevant):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
disable-servers = ["dodder", "nebulous"]
.Ed
.Pp
The two servers stay defined globally but are not spawned for sessions
under this directory subtree.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr moxy 1 ,
.Xr moxy-native 7 ,
.Xr toml 5
